{"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind"],"generated":true}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/benchmarks"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The benchmark suite measures the same workloads at several committed FirebladeECS revisions, such as a release tag against "},{"code":"main","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The workloads cover entity creation, destruction and lookup, adding and removing components, iterating families, system updates and component events. Revisions with value-type components run each workload on both the ","type":"text"},{"code":"archetype","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and the "},{"code":"sparseSet","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" storage (see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), so a report also shows what the storage choice costs."}]},{"text":"How results are made trustworthy","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"How-results-are-made-trustworthy"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each revision is built once and measured in "},{"code":"k","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" independent process replicates, interleaved in a seeded random order. The replicate is the unit of analysis: the centre value is the median of the replicate medians, with a distribution-free order-statistic 95% confidence interval. A speed-up against the baseline is the Hodges–Lehmann estimate with its exact confidence interval, tested with an exact Mann–Whitney test and adjusted across all comparisons of a report with Benjamini–Hochberg. A change counts as ","type":"text"},{"code":"faster","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"slower","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" only when it is significant and clears the ±5% equivalence zone; an interval inside that zone is reported as ","type":"text"},{"code":"equivalent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", anything else as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inconclusive"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Read-and-reproduce","text":"Read and reproduce"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The latest published report: ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/fireblade-engine.github.io\/ecs\/benchmarks\/","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Reports are published for dedicated benchmark releases only; the page shows the newest."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The 2.0.0 report: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/fireblade-engine.github.io\/ecs\/benchmarks\/2.0.0\/"},{"text":", the full suite with 10 replicates on both storages. Its source is committed as ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/fireblade-engine\/ecs\/blob\/main\/Documentation\/Benchmarks\/BenchmarkReport.html","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The statistical design and workload parity notes: "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/fireblade-engine\/ecs\/blob\/main\/Documentation\/Benchmarks\/Methodology.md","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To measure revisions locally, pass comma-separated tags, branches or commit IDs. Results are saved under ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Benchmarks\/Results\/<UTC timestamp>\/"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["make benchmark-compare REFS=1.4.3,main:2.0.0 REPLICATES=10 BENCHMARK_FILTER='.*'","make benchmark-report RESULTS=\"Benchmarks\/Results\/<run>\/*.json\" REPORT_BASELINE=1.4.3"],"syntax":"sh"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Without ","type":"text"},{"code":"BENCHMARK_FILTER","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" only 16 entities of every workload plus ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"entity.create.no-entities"},{"text":" (which only has 0 entities) run. ","type":"text"},{"code":"make benchmark-report","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" renders the single file ","type":"text"},{"code":"BenchmarkReport.html","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from saved results and never runs benchmarks. See ","type":"text"},{"code":"Benchmarks\/README.md","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for all options.","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"FirebladeECS"}],"title":"Benchmarks","roleHeading":"Article"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Benchmarks","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"See how FirebladeECS revisions compare on a shared 